# Moonstone, Harsh Mistress: "you may exile that card from your graveyard" - a card that is no longer in the graveyard when the
# trigger resolves is not the card any more (CR 400.7), so nothing is offered for it. Faithless Looting discards a Lightning Bolt
# and a Forest, two triggers go on the stack, and Bot2 answers with a Ghost Vacuum that exiles the Forest from the graveyard.
# Bot1's single Accept goes to the one prompt that is made, for the Bolt; if a prompt were made for the Forest as well it would take
# that Accept. The Bolt is then cast from exile with the Ruby on turn 5, its permission lasting through that turn; the Forest stays in
# exile as the Vacuum's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Moonstone, Harsh Mistress
Faithless Looting
Swamp
Lightning Bolt
Forest
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Ghost Vacuum
Island x15

